base-de-donnees-vps :

- Since the DNS cutover on 2026-09-10, the **live** MongoDB is the one
  self-hosted on the OVH VPS (135.125.226.16, `127.0.0.1:27017`, systemd
  service `blue-intelligence`). MongoDB Atlas is **frozen** at the
  pre-cutover state and no longer receives writes.
- **NEVER run `infra/vps/sync-from-atlas.sh`**: it would overwrite recent
  VPS data with the stale Atlas snapshot. The script has a lock
  (`FORCE_RESYNC`) — do not bypass it without an explicit user decision,
  with full awareness of the data loss.
- Data restore: use only the VPS daily local backups (`~/backups/mongodb/`,
  14-day rotation) — procedure in `infra/vps/README.md`.
